-- Karazhan Crypt (map 800): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), re-exported from turtle-agent feat/offmesh-links 2756955
-- (dungeons/karazhan_crypt.json) once the shaft dive was mapped. This file replaces the rows of 20261024021100: the plan row, its six
-- legs and all 275 steps are deleted and inserted again, and it carries NO ai_dungeon_boss row - the six bosses of map 800 were
-- seeded there and are unchanged (test_boss_table_is_the_seed holds that seed to one file).
--   turtle-agent plan-export --dir dungeons --mmaps <map 800 mmaps with the rebuilt 8005334> --allow-draft --approach-hops \
--     --rev 2756955 --stamp 20261025001100 karazhan_crypt
-- The rebuilt tile 8005334 (md5 6a8168b1d173551393bbeb75e4bb79d, offMeshConCount 2) carries the two off-mesh links of
-- KARAZHAN-CRYPT-NAVMESH.md: a dive from the south ramp foot (-11221.3 -1568.3 -3.67) to the shaft floor (-11221.3 -1560 -45.87), and
-- the swim across the shaft (-11213.1 -1572.3 -2.82) -> (-11207.3 -1510.4 -3.82). It is live on m910q only; the rows below were
-- checked and exported against a copy of the agent's mmaps with that one tile replaced (~/TortoiseBots-audit/kc-mmap/8005334.mmtile).
-- What changed (the dive route; evidence in ~/TortoiseBots-audit/tests/r39kc/, probe 2026-10-25):
--   * leg 1 (marrowspike) no longer starts at the lower crypt (-11194.2 -1796.4 -28.5). Its `to` is a DRY point on the south ramp
--     above the waterline (-11219.96 -1586.82 4.13; the shaft's water surface is 3.046), and its first approach row is ONE move
--     through the dive link to the shaft floor (-11221.3 -1560 -45.9): 56.8 yd straight, inside the run leader's 60 yd sight
--     distance. A bot did that dive live in 9 s (05:25:12 -> 05:25:30, gps.log) and the server's own .mmaps path answers Type 1
--     through the link from the walkway (pA-shaftfloor.txt, 37 points) - the move must START DRY, a water-to-water move is what the
--     bots' mover refuses (BFD C2/C3).
--   * the four Drowned Sinners 91932 that swim AT the shaft floor (z -41.2 to -44.7) are pulled right after the landing, each from a
--     stand on the floor: they killed a bot parked there in 32 s (05:25:30 -> 05:26:02), so the pulls come first, not the walk on.
--   * the walk up the lower-crypt slope passes the Shadowblade Spectre 91918 at -11219.3 -1639.8 -31.9: the pack of two Risen Crypt
--     Guards and the Spectre (radius 11.1) is pulled from a stand on the slope at -11213.8 -1632 -34.3 BEFORE the walk past it (a bot
--     that walked on was stopped at y -1655 and died there, pB-legs.txt), and a stand row on the lower crypt's own floor
--     (-11211 -1689 -28.5) comes before its first pull. Every floor leg is under 60 yd straight.
--   * the Drowned Sinners of the water column (11 of the 16, z -1.5 to -36.9) are out of the plan: they swim where no floor is
--     within the tank's look view (plan-check: "no point of the path comes within the look view of the pack"), so no walk-up pull
--     reaches them. They are the only 91932 the plan leaves.
--   * the Crypt Fearfeaster 91922 of leg 3 is out too: its spawn (-11168.1 -1652.65 23.69) stands on an unmeshed ledge 18 yd above
--     the hall floor (no polygon for it; the floors under it are z 1.1 and -28.5), so no stand reaches it. The tomb-bat trigger
--     summons one on the entrance hall instead.
--   * leg 5 (corpsemuncher) keeps its 11 south-wing pulls; its Drowned Sinner groups are out (the floor ones are pulled in leg 1) and
--     its last pack moved to the wing's east side, where its stand is 5.6 yd from it instead of 23. Its `to` crosses the swim link:
--     Corpsemuncher's wing is a navmesh island with no other contact, and that link is water at both ends, which the mover refuses.
--     The leg is NOT runnable until a swim across the shaft works; `.bot run skip` past it meanwhile.
-- Plan check (turtle-agent plan-check, the revision above, the mmaps copy): 195 points, 0 failing, 117 warnings (106 estimated patrol
-- periods, 7 detours, 4 off-mesh links) and 114 run-leader hop notices. Before: the same plan on the server's 2026-10-11 tiles fails
-- 173 of 191 points (149 unreachable, 12 too far, 12 needs_walk); on the rebuilt tile it still failed 13 (the 12 needs_walk + 1 too
-- far), which is what this rework fixed.
--   * The 7 detours are packs whose way is 162-284 yd for a 30-45 yd straight line: they stand on another layer (the lower crypt ->
--     the spider room, the terraces -> the hall). They were invisible while those floors were unreachable; the run leader walks to
--     each pull row's own point, so its rows are sound, but the agent's own driver would find no firing position there.
--   * One of the 4 off-mesh warnings names a segment that is not a link: the ramp foot (-11221.3 -1568.3 -3.7) up to the walkway
--     (-11221.3 -1706.7 4.3), a 138 yd walk. The branch flags the corner at a link's far end, which for a link walked backwards (the
--     shaft floor -> the ramp foot) lands on the segment after it. The tile holds exactly two off-mesh polys (parsed from the file);
--     the rows are unaffected (the exporter cuts hops by corner distance, and the plan has no avoid box).
-- 6 legs, 275 steps (152 pulls, 117 moves, 6 bosses), 282 rows. Kept from 20261024021100: the plan row's kill_first list, the leg
-- order and the per-leg pull census (radii, patrol blocks with estimated periods, Midnight 91927 as Enkhraz's boss.first).

-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- karazhan_crypt: map 800, 6 legs, 275 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'karazhan_crypt';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'karazhan_crypt';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'karazhan_crypt';
